{
  "caveats": [
    "The ranges in (b) mix models, sizes, quantisations, one-card and two-card runs and, for llama.cpp, CPU offload: they describe what each engine did here, not a controlled comparison.",
    "Most vLLM runs predate the engine pin and ran on 0.26.0; the llama.cpp floating-tag runs predate the pin too, and the two pairs had drifted to different builds under that tag.",
    "llama.cpp ran with one slot in 9 of its 11 runs in (b), so its eight-request figure is close to serialised single-stream speed there.",
    "The paired rows in (a) compare two quantisations of the same weights (Q4_K_M GGUF against W4A16), not only two engines.",
    "VRAM is what vLLM reserved (gpu-memory-utilization) and what llama.cpp held after load, read by nvidia-smi 3 s after the server was ready and before any request; neither is what the model needs."
